# Drafted by Gemini (R20), edited. R20 hook: Geneva's plea (route A), Geneva's accusation (route B), and the accusation of the postmaster across her counter (route B, earlier).

~ plea
Narrator: A pale girl with lilac eyes comes pelting up the north lane, her skirts bunched tight in her fists. Her breath tears in her throat like dry paper.
geneva_fairchild [afraid]: Miss Theodora is dead on the post office floor. Please, the constable will blame the first strangers she sees, so you have to come look at her right now.
* Tell us what happened. -> plea_what
* Lead the way, we will come at once. -> plea_go
* We cannot come just yet. -> plea_wait

~ plea_what
geneva_fairchild [afraid]: I found her face down among the morning letters. Nothing is taken, nothing is broken, and there is not a mark on her, though I dare not say more in the street.
-> plea
~ plea_wait
geneva_fairchild [sad]: Please do not be long. I cannot bear to stay in that room alone with her.
-> END

~ plea_go
set rk_started
quest roving_rookery plea
geneva_fairchild [afraid]: Thank heavens. Follow me quickly, and keep your heads down.
Narrator: You hurry after her down the narrow lane to where the post office door gapes open onto a cold, unlit room.
move wickermoor_post_office

~ geneva_accuses
Narrator: Pine torches sputter in the damp at the lane's end, and Geneva steps out before the whole massed village.
geneva_fairchild [angry]: There they are, the butchers who plotted to murder Mayor Somerton and spilled poor Theodora's secrets! We have your letter in hand, and you will answer for every word!
set hysteria_began = now
set rk_posse_out
quest roving_rookery posse
* [Insight DC 16] Study the lilac glint in her eyes, like someone standing behind them. -> geneva_charmed | geneva_missed
* We never laid a finger on the mayor. -> geneva_end
* Say nothing and look for a way out. -> geneva_end

~ geneva_charmed
set rk_charm_seen
Narrator: That lilac glint burns in her eyes and in every pair of eyes behind her, steady as a marsh lantern. This is no honest fury: it is a cold hand working a row of puppets.
-> geneva_end
~ geneva_missed
Narrator: For all your squinting through the torchlight, you see only a terrified young woman and a lane full of angry neighbours.
-> geneva_end
~ geneva_end
cutscene rk_village_turns
geneva_fairchild [angry]: The constable will hear what you have to say. Do not try to run.
cutscene rk_village_turns_2
Narrator: High along every wet roof ridge, rows of grey pigeons pivot their heads as one to fix you with their bead-black eyes.
cutscene end
-> END

~ accuse_theodora
Narrator: Theodora stands trim behind her counter with her gloved left hand flat on the open ledger, while the fat pigeon on her shoulder watches you without blinking.
theodora_mayville [neutral]: Good evening to you, travellers. Have you a parcel for the post, or only a letter that wants a clean seal?
* [Investigation DC 15] Lay out the mismatched seals, the altered letters, and her unremoved glove. -> exposed | exposed
* [Intimidation DC 16] We know what you are, and you have one chance to confess. -> exposed | exposed
* You are the hag who has been reading this valley's mail. -> exposed
* Post a letter and keep our suspicions to ourselves. -> accuse_wait

~ accuse_wait
theodora_mayville [neutral]: There you are, stamped and sorted. Do come again when you have news worth sending.
-> END

~ exposed
theodora_mayville [angry]: Oh, clever little strays, poking your noses into my pigeonholes! This whole valley was mine to pluck, and it will weep feathers before I am done with it!
Narrator: The postmaster sags behind the counter like an old coat slipped off a peg, a thick reek of wet feathers fills the room, and outside the north window something round heaves up on scaly pigeon legs.
cutscene rk_master_stroke_2
Narrator: Beyond the glass, the great dovecote rises on legs as thick as birch trunks, while Theodora's empty skin lies crumpled on the floorboards.
cutscene rk_master_stroke_3
Narrator: The rookery hops once, twice, and stalks away across the groaning roofs toward the dark moors, leaving its mischief behind for the valley to keep.
cutscene end
set golub_exposed
set golub_exposed_early
set geneva_alive
quest roving_rookery exposed
-> END
